From: Playtendoh
Subject: [PATCH] Libretro: the controller in each port as an input descriptor, the game database's too

On an "Auto" port Mesen plugs in what its game database (or an NES 2.0 header) says the game needs: the
Arkanoid paddle for Arkanoid, the Zapper for Duck Hunt, the Power Pad. A frontend could not tell, and so
could not give the paddle or the light gun anything from its own controller. Each port with a controller
other than a pad now has a descriptor of its own whose device is that controller's (DEVICE_ARKANOID,
DEVICE_ZAPPER...). RetroArch reads only the joypad's and analog's descriptors, so it is unchanged.

---
diff --git a/Libretro/libretro.cpp b/Libretro/libretro.cpp
index 48fa641..77dc6c9 100644
--- a/Libretro/libretro.cpp
+++ b/Libretro/libretro.cpp
@@ -816,7 +816,14 @@ extern "C" {
 			desc.push_back(d);
 		};
 
-		auto setupPlayerButtons = [addDesc](int port) {
+		//The controller in each port, the game database's on an "Auto" port too, as a descriptor of its own: a
+		//frontend that shows it, or maps its own input to it (a light gun, the Arkanoid paddle), can tell
+		auto addDevice = [&desc](unsigned port, unsigned device) {
+			retro_input_descriptor d = { port, device, 0, 0, "Controller" };
+			desc.push_back(d);
+		};
+
+		auto setupPlayerButtons = [addDesc, addDevice](int port) {
 			unsigned device = _inputDevices[port];
 			if(device == DEVICE_AUTO) {
 				if(port <= 3) {
@@ -850,6 +857,10 @@ extern "C" {
 				}
 			}
 
+			if(device != DEVICE_AUTO && device != RETRO_DEVICE_NONE && device != DEVICE_GAMEPAD && device != DEVICE_SNESGAMEPAD) {
+				addDevice(port, device);
+			}
+
 			if(device == DEVICE_GAMEPAD || device == DEVICE_SNESGAMEPAD) {
 				addDesc(port, RETRO_DEVICE_ID_JOYPAD_LEFT, "D-Pad Left");
 				addDesc(port, RETRO_DEVICE_ID_JOYPAD_UP, "D-Pad Up");
